text is in the file LICENSE.


Components the engine is built with
-----------------------------------

libslic3r (the Git submodule upstream/libslic3r, taken from the fork
https://github.com/dinamicby/OrcaSlicer)
    OrcaSlicer's slicing library, which descends from Bambu Studio, PrusaSlicer
    and Slic3r. License: GNU AGPL, version 3 (AGPL-3.0). The text is in
    upstream/libslic3r/LICENSE.txt. The commit built against is the libslic3r
    hash in REVISION.

OpenCASCADE Technology (OCCT), version 7.6.0
    Built from the source that upstream/libslic3r/deps downloads and linked into
    the engine: statically on macOS, as the shared libraries TK*.dll on Windows.
    License: GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1, with the Open
    CASCADE exception. https://dev.opencascade.org

MCUT (upstream/libslic3r/deps_src/mcut)
    Mesh cutting library, used by libslic3r. MCUT is offered under two mutually
    exclusive licenses; the engine uses it under option (A), the GNU General
    Public License, version 3 (GPL-3.0). See
    upstream/libslic3r/deps_src/mcut/LICENSE.txt and LICENSE.GPL.txt.

manifold-rust 0.10, a Rust port of the Manifold geometry library
    Cargo dependency of the engine (crates/slicer-geometry). License: Apache
    License, version 2.0. https://github.com/larsbrubaker/manifold-rust

Other libraries
    libslic3r is built from, and with, further libraries: those in
    upstream/libslic3r/deps_src, and those that upstream/libslic3r/deps
    downloads and builds (for example Boost, oneTBB, OpenVDB, NLopt, Qhull,
    OpenSSL and zlib). Each one is under its own license, which comes with its
    source; the licenses of the Rust crates the engine depends on are listed
    by the crates themselves and fixed by Cargo.lock.


Bundled presets
---------------

profiles/ holds presets merged from OrcaSlicer vendor profiles. Their origin
and terms are in profiles/LICENSE.md.


